    <other_details id="References">Archetypes: openEHR-EHR-FOLDER.generic.v1. CKM publishes no archetype for this class. The archetype id is the one EHRbase gives an instance of it by default, so a template on it validates what a CDR creates.</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>A generic folder: the archetype id openEHR-EHR-FOLDER.generic.v1, with any ITEM_TREE as its details, plain or defined by an archetype, and any sub-folders and items.</purpose>
      <keywords>folder</keywords>
      <keywords>directory</keywords>
      <keywords>default</keywords>
      <use>Install it on a CDR whose EHRs carry folders with no structure of their own, to build a default folder, and to validate a FOLDER that names it.</use>
      <misuse>Not where a folder's details must follow one structure, or its sub-folders or items have a structure of their own: use a template that constrains them.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openehr-reference-content contributors</copyright>
    </details>
